<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Martin Schongauer</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1448–1491</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Martin Schongauer was an Alsatian painter and engraver of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/colmar">Colmar</a>, the most important printmaker north of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alps">Alps</a> before <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/albrecht-durer">Albrecht Dürer</a>. His <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/copper">copper</a> engravings circulated widely across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>, and his painting the Madonna of the Rose Bower of 1473 survives in Colmar's Dominican church. He died in Breisach in 1491.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/martin-schongauer.jpg" alt="Martin Schongauer" width="320" height="447" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hans Burgkmair the Elder · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hans_Burgkmair_d.%C3%84._-_Bildnis_Martin_Schongauer_(Kopie).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
